<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grote Brief</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1187">1187</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gros Brief</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grote Brief ('Great Account') is the general account of the revenues of the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> for the year 1187, drawn up by the count's central financial officials. It lists the income in money and kind from the comital domains across the county and is one of the earliest surviving princely financial accounts in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, showing how advanced the administration of twelfth-century Flanders was.</p></div>
